1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:07,610
A Real Stewart

2
00:00:07,610 --> 00:00:09,830
Thanks, Michelle.

3
00:00:09,830 --> 00:00:19,750
I hope you like it.

4
00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:23,650
Isn't this baby outfit adorable?

5
00:00:23,650 --> 00:00:27,090
With his name on it--"Max."

6
00:00:27,090 --> 00:00:29,190
Thanks so much, Harry and Michelle.

7
00:00:29,190 --> 00:00:30,730
We really appreciate it.

8
00:00:30,730 --> 00:00:31,810
I'm glad you like it.

9
00:00:31,810 --> 00:00:32,690
Michelle picked it out.

10
00:00:32,690 --> 00:00:35,210
Yes, I told Daddy to pick blue ones.

11
00:00:35,210 --> 00:00:37,490
Blue is for boys, and pink is for girls.

12
00:00:37,490 --> 00:00:39,920
And Max is some boy.

13
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:41,650
He's a real Stewart.

14
00:00:41,650 --> 00:00:43,650
Right.

15
00:00:43,650 --> 00:00:46,350
That was so thoughtful of you, Michelle.

16
00:00:46,350 --> 00:00:49,300
Especially to pick it out in blue.

17
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:52,160
Would you like to see baby Max, Michelle?

18
00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:53,960
Could she? Could we?

19
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:55,130
Could I?

20
00:00:55,130 --> 00:00:56,620
Take them upstairs, Susan.

21
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:58,400
Harry and Michelle can watch Max sleeping.

22
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:02,210
Let's go.

23
00:01:02,210 --> 00:01:05,640
Come on, Michelle.

24
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:06,650
Before Max wakes up.

25
00:01:06,650 --> 00:01:08,450
Will you please take this upstairs, Susan?

26
00:01:08,450 --> 00:01:08,950
Uh-huh.

27
00:01:08,950 --> 00:01:13,970
Thank you.

28
00:01:13,970 --> 00:01:18,370
Michelle is very grown up for a ten-year-old, huh?

29
00:01:18,370 --> 00:01:22,160
She's smart and sensitive for her age.

30
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:25,000
Growing up without a mother is difficult.

31
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,380
You mature quickly.

32
00:01:28,380 --> 00:01:31,440
Susan's like a mother to Michelle.

33
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:35,330
They have a good relationship.

34
00:01:35,330 --> 00:01:41,270
Do you think Susan and Harry will get married?

35
00:01:41,270 --> 00:01:44,680
Yeah. You can count on it.

36
00:01:44,680 --> 00:01:47,550
I think so. Yes. They get along so well.

37
00:01:47,550 --> 00:01:51,420
I like him. He's good for Susan.

38
00:01:51,420 --> 00:01:54,140
He's a little quiet.

39
00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:58,320
It's hard to do anything but listen in this family.

40
00:01:58,320 --> 00:01:59,160
You're right, Ellen.

41
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:05,530
Oh, really?

42
00:02:05,530 --> 00:02:06,990
It's the way it should be.

43
00:02:06,990 --> 00:02:08,450
The Stewarts are the Stewarts!

44
00:02:08,450 --> 00:02:09,530
They always were,

45
00:02:09,530 --> 00:02:10,790
and they always will be.

46
00:02:10,790 --> 00:02:11,460
Right!

47
00:02:11,460 --> 00:02:13,520
They've always got an opinion.

48
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:16,590
Always got something to say.

49
00:02:16,590 --> 00:02:19,160
And now there's Max Stewart.

50
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:21,890
and if he talks as loudly as he cries,

51
00:02:21,890 --> 00:02:24,390
we're all in for trouble.

52
00:02:24,390 --> 00:02:25,750
He's quiet now.

53
00:02:25,750 --> 00:02:39,380
Mmm-hmm. That's because he's sleeping.

54
00:02:39,380 --> 00:02:42,170
He's really cute.

55
00:02:42,170 --> 00:02:44,260
It's not necessary to whisper, Harry.

56
00:02:44,260 --> 00:02:46,110
A baby gets used to voices.

57
00:02:46,110 --> 00:02:47,330
I remember now.

58
00:02:47,330 --> 00:02:49,770
We always whispered when Michelle was born.

59
00:02:49,770 --> 00:02:51,620
And I didn't sleep well, Daddy told me.

60
00:02:51,620 --> 00:02:52,440
I never slept.

61
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:53,170
And when I did,

62
00:02:53,170 --> 00:02:55,310
I woke up when I heard someone speak.

63
00:02:55,310 --> 00:02:57,150
I bet you were cute.

64
00:02:57,150 --> 00:02:58,270
She sure was.

65
00:02:58,270 --> 00:02:59,870
Not as cute as Max.

66
00:02:59,870 --> 00:03:14,610
He's like a little doll.

67
00:03:14,610 --> 00:03:15,650
Oh, good.

68
00:03:15,650 --> 00:03:19,340
Now I can help diaper him.

69
00:03:19,340 --> 00:03:23,610
Let's get Marilyn.

70
00:03:23,610 --> 00:03:25,390
What do you do when he cries like that?

71
00:03:25,390 --> 00:03:28,700
You pick him up.

72
00:03:28,700 --> 00:03:34,160
He's so little ... so new.

73
00:03:34,160 --> 00:03:38,080
Let's call Marilyn.

74
00:03:38,080 --> 00:04:07,590
Time for a feeding and time for a diapering.

75
00:04:07,590 --> 00:04:10,590
You're a real Stewart.
